        "name": "Spectral Hardness Verification",
        "pseudocode": "Algorithm: VerifySpectralHardness(f, C, x, y)\nInput: Attack function f, Certificate C = (p_1,...,p_k), pair (x,y)\nOutput: True if f is certified collision-resistant on (x,y)\n\n1. Verify certificate validity:\n   For i = 1 to k:\n     Assert \u00ac(x ~_{p_i} y)  (each prime separates)\n2. Check congruence reflection:\n   For i = 1 to k:\n     For all a, b in domain:\n       If p_i(f(a), f(b)) then assert p_i(a, b)\n3. If all checks pass:\n   By Theorem 5.1, f(x) \u2260 f(y) is guaranteed\n   Return True\n4. Else:\n   Return False (f is not in the reflecting attack class)\n\nComplexity: O(k \u00b7 |S|\u00b2) for reflection check"
