        "pseudocode": "Algorithm BerggrenHash(w, N, v\u2080):\n  Input: Word w = (g\u2081, ..., g\u2097), modulus N, base vector v\u2080 \u2208 (\u2124/N\u2124)\u00b3\n  Output: Hash h \u2208 (\u2124/N\u2124)\u00b3 satisfying h\u2080\u00b2 + h\u2081\u00b2 \u2261 h\u2082\u00b2 (mod N)\n\n  v \u2190 v\u2080\n  for i = \u2113 downto 1:\n    v \u2190 (M_{g\u1d62} \u00b7 v) mod N\n  return v\n\n  Complexity: O(9\u2113) modular multiplications\n  Invariant: output always Pythagorean mod N"
